From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 22:56:39 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] lavfi/overlay_vulkan: keep the main input's timebase on the
 output

The filter labels its output with one timebase and fills it with
timestamps expressed in another, so every output timestamp is wrong
whenever the two inputs do not already agree on one.

ff_framesync_configure() derives fs->time_base as the gcd of the
synchronised inputs' timebases, and framesync_inject_frame() rewrites
each arriving frame's pts into it. overlay_vulkan_blend() then copies
that rewritten pts onto the output frame with av_frame_copy_props(),
while the output link still carries the timebase ff_filter_config_links()
defaulted it to, which is the main input's. Compositing a 1/1000 main
branch with a 30000/1001 overlay branch gives fs->time_base 1/30000, so
every output pts comes out 30 times too large; the factor is whatever
ratio the two branches happen to produce.

State the output timebase explicitly as the main input's and pin
framesync to it, as overlay, overlay_vaapi and overlay_cuda do. With
fs->time_base already set, ff_framesync_configure() skips the gcd and
the injected timestamps are in the units the output link declares.
Signed-off-by: gregordinary <33880035+gregordinary@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 libavfilter/vf_overlay_vulkan.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/libavfilter/vf_overlay_vulkan.c b/libavfilter/vf_overlay_vulkan.c
index 1f9eed8..31efc9a 100644
--- a/libavfilter/vf_overlay_vulkan.c
+++ b/libavfilter/vf_overlay_vulkan.c
@@ -263,10 +263,14 @@ static int overlay_vulkan_config_output(AVFilterLink *outlink)
     if (err < 0)
         return err;
 
+    outlink->time_base = avctx->inputs[0]->time_base;
+
     err = ff_framesync_init_dualinput(&s->fs, avctx);
     if (err < 0)
         return err;
 
+    s->fs.time_base = outlink->time_base;
+
     return ff_framesync_configure(&s->fs);
 }
 
